# =============================================================================
# octeti odd digit count — An octeti literal needs two hex digits per byte.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • Every byte in an octeti hex literal is exactly two hex digits (|de ad be ef|)
#   • |686| has three digits, so no byte boundary exists — SEM011 rejects it by name
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Writing |686| and expecting the lone digit to pad — each byte needs exactly two digits
#
# See also: octeti, b8
# =============================================================================

# octeti odd-digit reject case — expected compile failure
#
